  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan AR01 July 2025\rBlock Plan AR02 July 2025\rExisting Ground Floor Plan Existing First Floor Plan AR03 July 2025\rProposed Ground Floor Plan Proposed First Floor Plan AR04 July 2025\rExisting Second Floor Plan Existing Roof Plan AR05 July 2025\rProposed Second Floor Plan Proposed Roof Plan AR06 July 2025\rExisting Section A-A AR07 July 2025\rProposed Section A-A AR08 July 2025\rExisting Front & Rear Elevations AR09 July 2025\rProposed Front & Rear Elevations AR10 July 2025\rExisting Side Elevations AR11 July 2025\rProposed Side Elevations AR12 July 2025\rPlanning Design Access and Heritage Statement P1237 July 2025\rHouse in Multiple Occupation Management Plan \rHighway Safety Impact Form\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than seven residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the cycle parking indicated on drawing 'Block Plan AR02 dated July 2025', and within six months of the date of this permission, cycle parking shall be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\ro Provision of a minimum of SEVEN long stay cycle parking spaces.\r\ro in an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m;\r\ro secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\ro fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking.",
    "Within six months of the date of this permission, details of facilities for the storage of recycling containers, wheeled refuse bins, and any other refuse storage containers including their materials and design specifications shall be submitted in writing to the local planning authority for approval.  Such details shall be implemented within 12 months of the date of this permission and maintained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To ensure that sufficient provision at all times for the storage and collection of waste and to preserve the character and appearance of the conservation area.\r"
  ],
